WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:07.700
Let's go next to our caller from the six six
one area code who's calling today from six

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.200
six one.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.040
A David, a long time viewer here from Lancaster,
California.

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:18.480
And I just had a quick question for you.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:19.800
Sure.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:28.190
The rhetoric that Trump and his campaign has
put forth since his election, since he started

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:37.629
running in 2015, I feel as though it's directly
led to a rise in deaths of despair in America.

00:00:37.629 --> 00:00:44.030
Alcohol, liver disease, suicide, drug overdose.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:49.440
And also, just overall, violent crimes, hate
crimes, things like that.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:58.249
And I actually wanted to know if you had any
thoughts on that.

00:00:58.249 --> 00:00:59.249
Any will.

00:00:59.249 --> 00:01:00.760
No, I have no particular thought.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.329
I mean, so there's a couple different sides
to that.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:09.550
So depths of despair often are related to
economic circumstances.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:15.230
And certainly it would be a counterpoint to
the idea that before Corona virus, things

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:16.230
were better than ever.

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:21.000
Because if things were better than ever, you
would not expect many of these deaths of despair

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.000
to be on the increase.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:29.220
Now, in terms of the hate crimes and crimes
targeting religious minorities or ethnic minorities

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:31.380
or whatever the case may be.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:37.030
I've said before, I don't think Trump has
created racists or xenophobes.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:41.070
And whether Trump is personally racist or
xenophobic is less relevant.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:49.160
What matters is Trump has made existing racists
and xenophobes more comfortable to be out

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:52.130
in public with their views and has emboldened
them.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:54.470
And so it's also not particularly surprising.

00:01:54.470 --> 00:02:00.070
But I think the deaths of despair are sort
of a different phenomena than that than some

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:03.310
of these hate crimes and other violence.

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:10.879
I appreciate the answer and they come on the
show and hope you have a good day.

00:02:10.879 --> 00:02:11.879
All right.

00:02:11.879 --> 00:02:12.879
Thank you.

00:02:12.879 --> 00:02:13.879
Yes, that that was the audio quality.

00:02:13.879 --> 00:02:14.879
There was brutal.

00:02:14.879 --> 00:02:14.883
I apologize for that.

